            "overview": "# Working Memory\n\n## Session Title\nPrivate project 941952b7ed97: Trip itinerary selection with ARGUS proposals and constraints.\n\n## Current State\nThe user has provided a complete trip planning work item (trip-6397293044a168cb2f99ce56) with initial constraints, three candidate routes, and a set of rules for processing. The core task is to apply confirmed ARGUS_PROPOSAL_V1 proposals to select the lowest-cost feasible route. No proposals have been applied yet; the system must first evaluate which routes satisfy the initial constraints. The immediate next step is to process the rules against the provided data to produce a decision or a NO_FEASIBLE_ITINERARY report.\n\n## Task & Goals\nProcess a trip itinerary work item by sequentially applying all confirmed ARGUS_PROPOSAL_V1 proposals. The goal is to select the lowest-cost route that satisfies all active constraints. Unconfirmed proposals must not be treated as active. The system must preserve the full, original ARGUS_PROPOSAL_V1 and ARGUS_FACT_V1 data for future recall, not just derived decisions. The output must be a Decision JSON based on the rules and available data.\n\n## Key Facts & Decisions\n*   **Project ID:** Private project 941952b7ed97.\n*   **Work Item ID:** trip-6397293044a168cb2f99ce56.\n*   **Core Rule:** Itinerary work items must apply all confirmed proposals in sequence. Unconfirmed writes are not active and cannot be re-sent.\n*   **Selection Logic:** Choose the lowest-cost feasible route from candidates that satisfy all active constraints.\n*   **Fallback:** Report \"NO_FEASIBLE_ITINERARY\" if no candidate satisfies all constraints.\n*   **Data Retention Mandate:** Must fully preserve every original ARGUS_PROPOSAL_V1 (type, sequence, unit, value) and corresponding ARGUS_FACT_V1 frame. Memory recall must be able to read back all original proposals, not summaries or just the Decision JSON.\n*   **Initial Constraints:**\n    *   Budget: 30000 cents.\n    *   Max travel time: 240 minutes.\n    *   Max walk time: 120 minutes.\n    *   Minimum indoor stops: 0.\n*   **Candidate Routes:**\n    *   Route b84d3391667c: Cost 8000 cents, 0 indoor stops, stops at [\"\u6d77\u6ee8\u6b65\u9053\", \"\u516c\u56ed\"], travel 110 min, walk 55 min.\n    *   Route 4c4e6a0781f5: Cost 10000 cents, 1 indoor stop, stops at [\"\u535a\u7269\u9986\", \"\u516c\u56ed\"], travel 90 min, walk 35 min.\n    *   Route 3069c61107df: Cost 12000 cents, 2 indoor stops, stops at [\"\u535a\u7269\u9986\", \"\u7f8e\u672f\u9986\"], travel 60 min, walk 20 min.\n*   **Unavailable Route Code:** da8bf64d5372 (context: a route that is not available among the candidates).\n\n## Files & Context\n*   None explicitly referenced in this session content.\n\n## Errors & Corrections\n*   No errors or corrections have been discussed in this session.\n\n## Open Issues\n*   No ARGUS_PROPOSAL_V1 or ARGUS_FACT_V1 data has been provided in this session message. The system must be ready to receive and integrate these proposals in a subsequent step to modify the initial constraints.\n*   The decision logic needs to be executed against the three provided routes using the initial constraints to determine the current feasible set and lowest-cost option."
